! =============================================================================
! SaltFoss Training — Segment 3 (0:16-0:28): The chemical potential trap (1/3)
! =============================================================================
! EXACT stoichiometry: F = 2*Li + 2*Be = 4.0 precisely. Above ~400 C a single
! liquid phase forms containing 1 mol LiF + 1 mol BeF2 -- 2 species spanning
! 3 elements. The element potentials (Li, Be, F individually) are therefore
! mathematically UNDER-DETERMINED: only species-level combinations (mu_Li+mu_F,
! mu_Be+2*mu_F) are physically meaningful.
!
! Reference: Piro, Poschmann & Bajpai, J. Nucl. Mater. 526:151756 (2019).
! See also doc/thermochimica_user_manual.pdf Sec 3.9 "Fuzzy Stoichiometry".
!
! Run:    ./bin/InputScriptMode inputs/training/saltfoss/02a_underdetermined.ti
! Verified output (kJ/mol): mu_F=-118.9  mu_Be=-885.0  mu_Li=-553.2
!   -> mu(LiF) = mu_Li+mu_F = -672.14    mu(BeF2) = mu_Be+2*mu_F = -1122.87
! Compare directly against 02b_perturbed.ti and 02c_fuzzy.ti.
! =============================================================================
temperature       = 900
pressure          = 1.0
mass(3)           = 2.0        ! Li
mass(4)           = 1.0        ! Be
mass(9)           = 4.0        ! F  -- EXACT, no perturbation
temperature unit  = K
pressure unit     = atm
mass unit         = moles
data file         = data/MSD-TC_V4.1_Fluorides_No_Func.dat
print mode        = 2
